WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.919 --> 00:00:16.400
at the tiny frozen woman.

2
00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:19.221
"That must be the Roodian queen!"

3
00:00:19.481 --> 00:00:20.142
she exclaimed.

4
00:00:20.882 --> 00:00:24.164
Zann spun around, his eyes searching the icy cave.

5
00:00:24.184 --> 00:00:26.165
"But where are my parents?"

6
00:00:26.405 --> 00:00:26.845
he cried.

7
00:00:26.865 --> 00:00:28.266
"They should be here!

8
00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:30.988
The queen was with them in my dream!"

9
00:00:31.816 --> 00:00:34.637
"Let's get the queen free, and maybe she can tell us."

10
00:00:35.437 --> 00:00:36.617
Venna turned to Wyssa.

11
00:00:36.637 --> 00:00:37.658
"What do you think?

12
00:00:38.358 --> 00:00:40.259
Should we try an Extraction spell?"

13
00:00:41.279 --> 00:00:42.959
Wyssa frowned and stroked her chin.

14
00:00:42.979 --> 00:00:47.181
"That could injure her if there are any imperfections in the ice.

15
00:00:48.101 --> 00:00:51.222
What about a Supplanting spell?"

16
00:00:52.062 --> 00:00:53.863
"Do you think you can manage that?"

17
00:00:54.183 --> 00:00:55.403
Venna sounded doubtful.

18
00:00:55.423 --> 00:01:02.265
"If we don't get the dimensions exactly right Zing bounded over and sniffed at the trapped queen.

19
00:01:02.985 --> 00:01:06.506
He whistled curiously, and a wisp of flame escaped his mouth.

20
00:01:06.526 --> 00:01:09.147
"Careful, Zing," Darb said.

21
00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:10.367
"Don't burn her."

22
00:01:10.387 --> 00:01:13.608
"No, wait, look."

23
00:01:13.828 --> 00:01:14.408
Gliss pointed.

24
00:01:14.428 --> 00:01:16.149
"He's melting the ice!"

25
00:01:16.169 --> 00:01:18.509
"Go, Zing," Zann urged.

26
00:01:18.529 --> 00:01:19.630
"Keep melting it!"

27
00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:23.611
The little dragon breathed on the block of ice, which quickly melted.

28
00:01:24.291 --> 00:01:26.011
Within seconds the queen was free.

29
00:01:27.912 --> 00:01:28.532
Perda grinned.

30
00:01:28.972 --> 00:01:29.973
"Good job, Zing.

31
00:01:30.313 --> 00:01:33.875
That was much easier than using any of those complicated spells."

32
00:01:33.895 --> 00:01:36.596
"Thank you!"

33
00:01:37.257 --> 00:01:40.719
the queen said breathlessly, shaking icy droplets from her clothes.

34
00:01:40.739 --> 00:01:42.339
"But please!

35
00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:44.260
You have to stop him!"

36
00:01:45.201 --> 00:01:45.821
Venna nodded.

37
00:01:45.841 --> 00:01:46.582
"We know.

38
00:01:47.002 --> 00:01:49.243
Morb already tried to take over Magica once."

39
00:01:50.044 --> 00:01:51.004
The queen shook her head.

40
00:01:51.024 --> 00:01:54.986
"He's not trying to take over your world this time," she said.

41
00:01:55.006 --> 00:01:57.728
"He's trying to destroy it!"

42
00:01:58.772 --> 00:02:00.393
"What?" Gliss exclaimed.

43
00:02:00.993 --> 00:02:01.673
"Destroy it?"

44
00:02:01.893 --> 00:02:02.414
Zann said.

45
00:02:02.434 --> 00:02:04.935
"How?" Venna shook her head.

46
00:02:04.955 --> 00:02:06.475
"Impossible," she said.

47
00:02:06.495 --> 00:02:11.237
"Yes, the Horn of the Otherworld is one of the most powerful relics known.

48
00:02:11.977 --> 00:02:16.239
But Morb is crazy if he thinks he can use it to destroy an entire world.

49
00:02:17.019 --> 00:02:18.880
It doesn't have that much power."

50
00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:22.522
"Not on its own," Wyssa said slowly.

51
00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:26.803
"Don't you know where the Horn came from originally?"

52
00:02:27.584 --> 00:02:28.284
Venna shrugged.

53
00:02:28.588 --> 00:02:30.809
"A faraway world of powerful magic.

54
00:02:31.149 --> 00:02:33.091
That's all the ancient texts say about it."

55
00:02:33.871 --> 00:02:35.032
"Where did it come from?"

56
00:02:35.152 --> 00:02:36.152
Perda asked Wyssa.

57
00:02:36.793 --> 00:02:37.653
Wyssa looked grim.

58
00:02:38.173 --> 00:02:41.435
"From the head of the Beast of the Otherworld."

59
00:02:41.455 --> 00:02:44.497
"What?" Gliss shuddered.

60
00:02:44.517 --> 00:02:47.078
"You mean that horrible thing outside?"

61
00:02:47.839 --> 00:02:48.579
Darb frowned.

62
00:02:48.599 --> 00:02:50.560
"But the Beast didn't have any horns."

63
00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:53.241
"Exactly," Wyssa said.

64
00:02:53.702 --> 00:02:57.704
"It originally had two horns growing from its head.

65
00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:05.322
According to legend, it fought a terrible battle long ago with a Forellian deathshifter.

66
00:03:06.102 --> 00:03:11.243
That's how it lost the horn you've seen, the one that later became a relic in Magica."

67
00:03:11.263 --> 00:03:13.404
"And the second horn?"

68
00:03:13.704 --> 00:03:14.244
Zann said.

69
00:03:14.944 --> 00:03:15.645
Wyssa shrugged.

70
00:03:15.665 --> 00:03:17.645
"That part is a mystery.

71
00:03:18.485 --> 00:03:21.506
The legends don't mention anything about the second horn.

72
00:03:22.306 --> 00:03:27.808
So as far as I know, the Beast still had it until very recently."

73
00:03:28.836 --> 00:03:30.557
"Yes," said the Roodian queen.

74
00:03:30.577 --> 00:03:36.281
"Recently Morb disabled the Beast long enough to cut off the remaining horn."

75
00:03:37.362 --> 00:03:42.786
Zann remembered the dark stuff dripping from the Beast's head and realized it must have been blood.

76
00:03:42.806 --> 00:03:45.948
"But how did Morb disable the Beast?"

77
00:03:46.268 --> 00:03:46.889
asked Darb.

78
00:03:47.569 --> 00:03:51.151
The queen pointed to the mibbit, which was peeking out from Darb's arms.

79
00:03:51.171 --> 00:03:53.933
"He used that creature."

80
00:03:53.953 --> 00:03:57.616
"Of course, I should have guessed," Wyssa muttered.

81
00:03:58.764 --> 00:04:05.027
"The mibbit is probably the only creature in all the known worlds that could overcome the Beast's powerful

82
00:04:05.147 --> 00:04:07.948
magic." "What about a scatter beast?"

83
00:04:08.288 --> 00:04:08.768
Venna said.

84
00:04:08.788 --> 00:04:11.809
"Well, yes, that would work too."

85
00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:13.670
Wyssa looked thoughtful.

86
00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:17.752
"But Morb would have trouble controlling a scatter beast safely.

87
00:04:18.632 --> 00:04:23.814
Since he's a Void, a mibbit would be—" A sudden whooshing sound cut her off.

88
00:04:24.535 --> 00:04:25.255
Gliss screamed.

89
00:04:25.575 --> 00:04:27.596
"Something just ripped my sleeve!"

90
00:04:28.552 --> 00:04:34.037
Zann ducked as a tiny shape zipped past his face, missing him by the width of a dragon's

91
00:04:34.097 --> 00:04:40.483
scale. Spinning around, he saw a lizard with a sharp blade for a snout, which was embedded in

92
00:04:40.523 --> 00:04:41.303
the icy wall.

93
00:04:42.064 --> 00:04:43.605
It was already pulling itself free.

94
00:04:43.625 --> 00:04:47.409
"Blade lizards from Redsea," Wyssa said.

95
00:04:47.429 --> 00:04:49.711
"Morb has always liked those."

96
00:04:49.731 --> 00:04:51.993
"Run!" Perda cried.

97
00:04:52.013 --> 00:04:54.415
"No, join hands!"

98
00:04:54.655 --> 00:04:55.256
Wyssa ordered.

99
00:04:55.648 --> 00:04:57.910
"Blade lizards are too fast.

100
00:04:58.210 --> 00:04:59.691
We have to zap away."

101
00:05:00.792 --> 00:05:02.913
Zap! Splash!

102
00:05:02.933 --> 00:05:05.215
"Drat!" said Zann.

103
00:05:05.235 --> 00:05:09.618
"I always His whole body froze before he could finish.

104
00:05:10.319 --> 00:05:15.322
Constant shocks were passing through him, making it impossible to move or even think.

105
00:05:15.342 --> 00:05:17.444
"Zann!" Perda cried.

106
00:05:17.464 --> 00:05:18.605
"What's wrong?"

107
00:05:18.625 --> 00:05:21.307
"Hold on, boy," Wyssa called.

108
00:05:21.327 --> 00:05:22.568
"I've got you."

109
00:05:23.344 --> 00:05:26.207
Zann felt himself being levitated out of the water.

110
00:05:26.807 --> 00:05:29.369
By the time he landed, the shocks were wearing off.

111
00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:31.791
Finally he could look around.

112
00:05:32.532 --> 00:05:36.655
The whole group was in a small courtyard with an ornate fountain in the middle.

113
00:05:37.496 --> 00:05:38.196
"What happened?"

114
00:05:38.437 --> 00:05:39.057
Zann asked.

115
00:05:39.077 --> 00:05:42.260
"Paralyzer pythons," Wyssa said.

116
00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:46.183
"It's a good thing you were the only one who landed in the water."

117
00:05:46.203 --> 00:05:50.827
"Yeah," Zann muttered, glancing at the creatures writhing in the fountain.

118
00:05:50.847 --> 00:05:51.888
"Good thing."

119
00:05:53.260 --> 00:05:55.522
"This is bad," Wyssa said.

120
00:05:55.542 --> 00:05:57.344
"It sure is!"

121
00:05:57.584 --> 00:05:58.304
Gliss exclaimed.

122
00:05:58.324 --> 00:06:02.408
"How many creatures does Morb have guarding this place, anyway?"

123
00:06:02.428 --> 00:06:05.791
"I'm not talking about the pythons, girl."

124
00:06:06.331 --> 00:06:08.153
Wyssa waved a hand dismissively.

125
00:06:08.173 --> 00:06:10.415
"I'm talking about Morb's plan.

126
00:06:11.095 --> 00:06:18.001
If he gets his hands on both horns at the same time, his power will be absolutely unimaginable."

127
00:06:19.282 --> 00:06:21.344
"Yes." Venna sounded anxious.

128
00:06:22.156 --> 00:06:27.519
"And thanks to that Possession spell he placed on me, the second horn is probably already here in

129
00:06:27.559 --> 00:06:30.261
Rood. But I still don't understand.

130
00:06:31.041 --> 00:06:34.323
How is he planning to use the horns to destroy Magica?"

131
00:06:35.023 --> 00:06:36.404
The Roodian queen spoke up.

132
00:06:36.424 --> 00:06:37.825
"I think I know.

133
00:06:38.745 --> 00:06:44.068
The servants here in the fortress have been whispering about a terrible contraption Morb is building.

134
00:06:45.069 --> 00:06:47.550
He calls it a Memory Eater."

135
00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:49.871
"That sounds familiar."

136
00:06:50.131 --> 00:06:50.992
Venna bit her lip.

137
00:06:51.392 --> 00:06:53.574
"I think it's mentioned in the ancient texts.

138
00:06:54.315 --> 00:06:55.876
But I'm not sure how it works."

139
00:06:56.737 --> 00:06:59.660
"Do you know any more about this contraption?"

140
00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:00.901
Wyssa asked the queen.

141
00:07:01.902 --> 00:07:06.587
"Only that Morb has brought prisoners from his home world to power it," the queen said.

142
00:07:06.607 --> 00:07:10.831
"A man and a woman named Nax and Asta."

143
00:07:11.692 --> 00:07:12.713
Zann gasped.

144
00:07:12.733 --> 00:07:14.054
"My parents!"
